
# Skill content ships to other people's machines and is compared byte for byte by the split
# migration gate, so its line endings must not depend on which platform last checked it out.
# Without this the copy step reported 16 of 41 destinations "not byte-identical" when the only
# difference was CRLF, twice, in opposite directions: once after a git stash round-trip rewrote the
# source tree, once after a commit rewrote the copies.
skills/**/*.md    text eol=lf
skills/**/*.json  text eol=lf

# The capability catalog records a BYTE COUNT for every source it measures. Eight of the nine
# are docs-mirror pages outside this repo; this one is a repo text file, so its size depended on
# which checkout produced it. A catalog generated in a CRLF worktree recorded 171459 bytes and
# --check then failed on an LF main reading 170559, exactly 900 apart, one byte per line, and it
# surfaced as DRIFT_UNCLASSIFIED because the mismatch is a size rather than any compared field.
# Same hazard, same fix, as the skills rule above.
tests/lint-bench/results.json  text eol=lf
